# Example article

This is a placeholder read-only article. It exists to prove the docs-site
framework: each acadamark source becomes one rendered page, the pages share a
navigation header, and a read-only page carries a "view source on GitHub"
link in its footer.

## Rendering Layer 1

Body text with some **emphasis**, a bit of `inline code`, and inline math
$f(x) = x^2$. acadamark renders these to semantic Layer 1 HTML, which the
default stylesheet themes into the finished look you see here.

## Block content

> A blockquote, to show block-level rendering distinct from body paragraphs.

Lists, math, quotes, and emphasis are all delegated to well-established
parsers; acadamark adds the scholarly vocabulary on top.

## Status

This is placeholder content for the Phase 14 Slice 3a framework. The real
articles — the project's README and DESIGN translated to canonical
acadamark — land in Slice 3b.
